PHASE 1: DevOps Foundation (Must Complete First)
Team: DevOps Engineer
Blocker: Infrastructure team needs this before ANY Terraform work
Tasks:

GitHub Repository Setup

Create repo structure (infra/, terraform/, ansible/, docs/)
Branch protection rules (main, develop)
README with project overview
.gitignore for secrets


GitHub Actions Self-Hosted Runner

Deploy runner VM (Ubuntu/RHEL)
Install prerequisites:

Terraform
Ansible
Node.js
AWS CLI
Python3 + pip


Configure runner with IP in infrastructure network range
Register runner to GitHub repo
Test workflow execution


AWS Account Foundation

Create/configure AWS account
Enable MFA on root account
Set up billing alerts


AWS IAM Users & Policies

Create Terraform automation user
Create DevOps team user
Create Infrastructure team user
Configure least-privilege IAM policies
Generate access keys
Store credentials in GitHub secrets


AWS S3 Backend for Terraform State

Create S3 bucket: <project>-terraform-state
Enable versioning
Enable encryption (AES-256 or KMS)
Configure bucket policy (restrict access)
Set up lifecycle rules


AWS DynamoDB for State Locking

Create table: terraform-state-lock
Configure read/write capacity
Test state locking


AWS Network Planning (Documentation Phase)

VPC CIDR blocks
Subnet design (public/private)
Route tables planning
ACL rules design
Security groups planning
VPN connectivity planning (for Phase 5)



Deliverables:

GitHub repo with runner configured
AWS account with S3/DynamoDB ready
Terraform backend configuration documented
Network architecture diagram for AWS

